Subject: [PATCH v2 10/16] src/lab-process-mail: Answer the list on lab-mail
To: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Cc: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: xrntqxrrwltkkxwqumvzzlmtouwrznus
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:33:35 +0000

The agent answered the jj maildir, so a reply reached the list only
once Pat merged the outbox commit that carried it. On lab-mail a reply
is on the list as soon as it is posted, and Pat no longer has to
merge mail.

A pass now syncs before it starts, posts series with git send-email
and replies with msmtp, and saves each reply by Fcc into sent. The
copy tags the message replied at once, so the loop still checks a
side effect the agent cannot fake by printing, without waiting for
the sync to bring the reply back.

The agent cannot file mail on lab-mail, so instead of quarantining
mail from unknown senders, the loop answers only approved senders
and logs the rest.

prompt.md and CLAUDE.md describe the new procedure, and the spec
records it.
